# ED360

## An intelligent business operating system for consultancy firms

**ED360** is an advanced CRM and business management platform designed specifically for consultancy businesses that need more than traditional lead management.

Instead of relying on separate tools for CRM, employee management, payroll, communication, reporting, and day-to-day operations, ED360 brings the core functions of a consultancy business into a single intelligent platform.

With advanced automation, AI-powered capabilities, integrations, centralized data, and operational dashboards, ED360 helps consultancy teams manage their entire business from one place.

---

# The Challenge

Consultancy businesses often operate across multiple disconnected systems.

Leads may be tracked in a CRM.
Employee information may live in spreadsheets.
Salary calculations may be handled manually.
Follow-ups can depend on individual employees remembering them.
Reports may require manually combining data from different sources.

As a business grows, this creates several problems:

* Scattered business data
* Manual administrative work
* Poor visibility into employee performance
* Missed lead follow-ups
* Repetitive operational tasks
* Difficulty tracking conversions
* Complicated salary management
* Limited real-time business insights
* Multiple disconnected software systems

ED360 was designed to solve this fragmentation.

---

# The Vision

### One platform. Every operation. Intelligent by default.

The goal behind ED360 was to create a centralized digital infrastructure for consultancy businesses.

Rather than simply recording customer information like a traditional CRM, ED360 connects different parts of the organization together.

A lead can move through the sales pipeline.

An employee can manage that lead.

The system can track the employee's performance.

The resulting business activity can contribute to reports and analytics.

Management can then use those insights to make better operational decisions.

This creates a connected business ecosystem rather than a collection of isolated tools.

